%description:

A deviation of the uplink from TR 38.901, recorded rather than fixed
(model-deviations.md item 33): a sectorial (ANISOTROPIC) base station's
antenna pattern is applied only when the base station transmits. When it
receives, the pattern is applied to nothing: not to its own UEs, and not to
the interfering UEs (computeUplinkInterference() takes getAttenuation(), which
has no angular term). So a sector hears the UEs behind it at full gain, which
matters most in three-sector sites, where every sector has two neighbours
pointing away from it.

TR 38.901 7.5 Step 1 d): "Give BS and UT antenna field patterns Frx and Ftx in
the global coordinate system and array geometries"; Frx is the "Receive
antenna element u field pattern". The pattern is Table 7.3-1's, so a UE 300 m
behind the sector arrives 29.943020172152938 dB weaker than one 300 m in
front, as in the downlink; the geometry and the expected value are those of
ChannelModelSectorPattern, which pins the current behaviour (no difference).

When fixed, drop the %expected-failure line, and change the pinned check of
ChannelModelSectorPattern into this one.

%expected-failure: the receive pattern of a sectorial base station is ignored in the uplink

%includes:
#include "SchedulerTestUtil.h"
#include "ChannelModelTestUtil.h"

%global:
using namespace simu5g;
using namespace simu5g::unittest;
using inet::Coord;

// The control information a packet from 'source' to 'dest' carries.
static UserControlInfo controlInfo(Direction dir, LtePhyFrameType type, MacNodeId source,
        MacNodeId dest)
{
    UserControlInfo info;
    info.setDirection(dir);
    info.setFrameType(type);
    info.setSourceId(source);
    info.setDestId(dest);
    return info;
}

%file: harness.ned
import simu5g.common.binder.Binder;
import simu5g.stack.phy.medium.CellularRadioMedium;
import simu5g.common.carrierAggregation.CarrierAggregation;
import simu5g.stack.phy.channelmodel.Tr38901ChannelModel;

network Harness
{
    submodules:
        binder: Binder;
        radioMedium: CellularRadioMedium;
        carrierAggregation: CarrierAggregation;
        model: Tr38901ChannelModel;
        test: Test;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini
[General]
network = Harness
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-log-prefix = ""
sim-time-limit = 1s

*.carrierAggregation.numComponentCarriers = 1
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].carrierFrequency = 3.5GHz
*.carrierAggregation.componentCarrier[0].numBands = 1
**.cellInfoModule = ""
*.binder.printTrafficGeneratorConfig = false

**.scenario = "URBAN_MICROCELL"
**.nodebHeight = 25m
**.ueHeight = 1.5m
**.dynamicLos = false
**.fixedLos = true
**.shadowing = false
**.fading = false

%no-default-inifile: 1

%activity:
Checker c;
auto *model = harnessModule<StochasticChannelModel>(this, "model");
auto *medium = harnessModule<CellularRadioMedium>(this, "radioMedium");

StubEndpoint bs, front, behind;
const MacNodeId bsId = MacNodeId(1), frontId = MacNodeId(1025), behindId = MacNodeId(1026);
bs.nodeId = bsId;
bs.coord = Coord(0, 0, 25);
bs.txDirection = ANISOTROPIC;
bs.txAngle = 0;
front.nodeId = frontId;
front.coord = Coord(300, 0, 1.5);
behind.nodeId = behindId;
behind.coord = Coord(-300, 0, 1.5);
StubRadioRegistration bsRadio(medium, bsId, &bs);
StubRadioRegistration frontRadio(medium, frontId, &front);
StubRadioRegistration behindRadio(medium, behindId, &behind);
ChannelModelProbe probe(model);

// TR 38.901 Table 7.3-1, A(theta, 0) - A(theta, 180) at theta = 90 + atan(23.5 / 300) deg
const double patternDifference = 29.943020172152938;

// TR 38.901 7.5 Step 1 d) and Table 7.3-1: the base station's receive pattern
UserControlInfo fromFront = controlInfo(UL, DATAPKT, frontId, bsId);
UserControlInfo fromBehind = controlInfo(UL, DATAPKT, behindId, bsId);
double ulFront = model->getRSRP(probe.linkFor(&bs, &fromFront, front.coord), 23.0)[0];
double ulBehind = model->getRSRP(probe.linkFor(&bs, &fromBehind, behind.coord), 23.0)[0];
c.expectNear("UL: the UE behind the sector arrives weaker by the pattern of TR 38.901 Table 7.3-1",
        ulFront - ulBehind, patternDifference, 1e-9);

c.summary();

%contains: stdout
modelchecks=1 modelfailures=0

%not-contains: stdout
FAILED
